I made a mess in the coverOf edit — I wrote nonsense (`findArchive().firstOrNull(Library.ARCHIVE_EXTENSIONS)` and a useless `collectUris`). Let me rewrite the cover logic properly and simply.

Plan for cover:
```kotlin
fun coverOf(uri: String): ByteArray? {
    // list children of folder
    val nodes = list(uri).sortedWith { a, b -> naturalOrder(a.name, b.name) }
    // 1) direct image files
    for (n in nodes) if (!n.isDirectory && n.extension in IMAGE_EXTENSIONS) {
        library.readBytes(n.uri)?.let { return it }
    }
    // 2) first archive in this folder (natural order) — its first image
    for (n in nodes) if (!n.isDirectory && n.extension in ARCHIVE_EXTENSIONS) {
        firstPageBytes(n.uri)?.let { return it }
    }
    // 3) descend into subfolders
    for (n in nodes) if (n.isDirectory) {
        coverOf(n.uri)?.let { return it }
    }
    return null
}
```
Wait, for a folder with a single archive file: coverOf(folder) → node is not image, not archive (it's a directory)... Actually `list(uri)` returns children. My earlier version used `list(uri).firstOrNull()` which is wrong — that's the first child, not the folder itself. Let me check how LibraryActivity calls it: for Item.Folder it passes item.uri (folder). For Item.Volume (archive or image) it passes the file uri. So coverOf must handle BOTH a file uri and a folder uri.

So:
```kotlin
fun coverOf(uri: String): ByteArray? = coverFile(uri) ?: coverFolder(uri)
```
But we don't know if `uri` is a file or folder without querying. Simpler: try firstPageBytes(uri) (works for archives), then readBytes(uri) (works for image files), then descend as folder. That handles all three cases:

```kotlin
fun coverOf(uri: String): ByteArray? {
    // Файл-архив: первая картинка из него.
    firstPageBytes(uri)?.let { return it }
    // Файл-картинка: она сама.
    library.readBytes(uri)?.let { return it }  // но это прочитает каталог? readBytes на папку вернёт null или исключение
    // Папка: первая картинка среди содержимого, иначе первый архив, иначе вглубь.
    val nodes = list(uri).sortedWith { a, b -> naturalOrder(a.name, b.name) }
    ...
}
```
For a folder, `firstPageBytes` will try openChannel → SAF returns a directory descriptor; FileChannel.read will throw → runCatching → null. `readBytes` on folder → openInputStream may throw → runCatching → null. Then list(uri) gives children. OK that works but does two failed IO per row. Acceptable.

Order preference: for a folder, prefer a direct image file (cheap) before opening an archive. But we can't know it's a folder until list() succeeds. Let me do list() first — if list returns empty/null → it's a file → read as archive/image.

```kotlin
fun coverOf(uri: String): ByteArray? {
    val children = runCatching { list(uri) }.getOrDefault(emptyList())
    if (children.isEmpty()) {
        // Это файл: архив или картинка.
        return firstPageBytes(uri) ?: library.readBytes(uri)
    }
    val ordered = children.sortedWith { a, b -> naturalOrder(a.name, b.name) }
    // 1) картинки прямо в папке — самая дешёвая обложка
    for (n in ordered) if (!n.isDirectory && n.extension in Library.IMAGE_EXTENSIONS) {
        library.readBytes(n.uri)?.let { return it }
    }
    // 2) первый архив папки: раскрываем центральный каталог один раз
    for (n in ordered) if (!n.isDirectory && n.extension in Library.ARCHIVE_EXTENSIONS) {
        firstPageBytes(n.uri)?.let { return it }
    }
    // 3) вложенные папки
    for (n in ordered) if (n.isDirectory) {
        coverOf(n.uri)?.let { return it }
    }
    return null
}
```
Note: `firstPageBytes` opens the zip channel, reads central directory — only for the first archive, not all. This makes covers fast and no title build.

Also remove the now-unused titleOfFolderCached? It's still used by... nothing else? coverOf was the only user. Let me keep titleByUri removal and the function only if used. I'll remove titleOfFolderCached and titleByUri if unused (check usages: pagesOf uses entries; title() doesn't use cache).

Also the grey covers: also add placeholder icon? Let's set a neutral background color and only show ImageView when a cover exists; otherwise show a small text of the title's first letter? Keep background gray (placeholder) but now covers should actually load.

Also "читалки не существует": add toast when pages empty; and make sure ReaderActivity has navigation. Let me also verify the subfolders-as-chapters issue: buildTitle ignores subdirs as volumes, so chapters show only archives/loose images flattened from all depths. Since collect recurses, chapters = all archives+images. That's why a folder with only subfolders shows chapters (from deeper levels). Good.

But wait — if a folder contains subfolders AND the user expects to browse, tapping folder opens Detail; Detail shows all chapters. OK.

One more real bug candidate: `collect` recursion requires `trees` map to have the subdir's URI → tree. Since collect calls list(child.uri) and list() records trees[childUri] when listing the parent — yes, parent's list() registered child URIs. Good.

Let me now fix the code properly and remove the junk I wrote.

